  "question": {
    "text": "A car is moving towards an approaching bike. the bike is moving with a velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msup><mtext>m&nbsp;s</mtext><mtext>-1</mtext></msup></math> . Frequency of horn sounded by the car is <math><mn>100</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mtext>H</mtext><mtext>z</mtext></math> , while it is observed by bike rider as <math><mn>120</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mtext>H</mtext><mtext>z</mtext></math> . The actual duration of horn is <math> <mrow> <mn>6</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mtext>s</mtext> </mrow> </math> . Find the time interval for which the bike rider hears it. (Take velocity of sound in air as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>330</mn><msup><mtext>&nbsp;m&nbsp;s</mtext><mtext>-1</mtext></msup></math>)",
